<p>
  The tax catalogues are transcriptions of real forms. One or more of those
  forms appears to have changed, so a catalogue may now be describing a document
  that no longer exists.
</p>

<% @findings.each do |f| %>
  <h3><%= f[:report_name] %> &mdash; <%= f[:kind].to_s.tr("_", " ") %></h3>
  <p><%= f[:message] %></p>
  <% if f[:detail].present? %><p><%= f[:detail] %></p><% end %>
  <p><%= link_to f[:url], f[:url] %></p>
<% end %>

<p>
  <strong>What to do:</strong> open the form, compare it against
  <code>db/tax_categories/</code>, and correct the catalogue in place. Then
  update the <code>source</code> checksum and <code>form_year</code> in its
  header.
</p>
<p>Nothing has changed automatically. This message is the only effect.</p>
